  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Hola (Ukrainian/Slavic partnership trick-taking). 4 players, 2 partnerships. Setup: 52-card deck, 4 cards per player, stockpile refills. Gameplay: Lead plays card. Others play any card. Win by matching lead rank OR playing 7/2 (wild). Countering allowed. Scoring: Aces (10) + Tens (10) + last trick (10) = 90 total. Hola (all 90) = 170 bonus. First partnership to target wins.',
    Player: "Welcome to Hola, the Ukrainian-Canadian classic. Play as partnerships in a unique trick-taking game. The lead plays a card. To win, play a card of the SAME RANK or use a wild (7 or 2). Your partner can counter an opponent's play to win the trick back. Capture Aces and Tens for points. Score all 90 points in a hand = Hola = bonus!",
    objective: "Score points by capturing Aces and Tens (the 'counting cards'). There are 90 total points available (8 counting cards + 10 for the last trick).",
    gameplay: "1. The lead player plays a card.\n2. In turn, others play ANY card. You do not have to follow suit.\n3. **Winning the Trick**: To beat the lead, you must play a card of the SAME RANK as the lead, or a WILD card (7 or 2).\n4. **Countering**: The lead player can respond by playing another card of the same rank or another wild card to 'take back' the trick. This continues until everyone has passed or played on the lead.\n5. The last player to match the lead rank (or play a wild) wins all cards in the trick.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Hola.',
      'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: - Aces: 10 points each.',
      "Winning condition: Score points by capturing Aces and Tens (the 'counting cards').",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4 players in two fixed partnerships (opponents sit opposite).',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Ranking: 7s and 2s are WILD.',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck. Ranking: 7s and 2s are WILD.',
      dealing: 'Deal 4 cards to each player. The remaining cards form a stockpile (Draw Pile). Each player refills their hand to 4 cards after every trick until the deck is gone.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. The lead player plays a card.\n2. In turn, others play ANY card. You do not have to follow suit.\n3. **Winning the Trick**: To beat the lead, you must play a card of the SAME RANK as the lead, or a WILD card (7 or 2).\n4. **Countering**: The lead player can respond by playing another card of the same rank or another wild card to 'take back' the trick. This continues until everyone has passed or played on the lead.\n5. The last player to match the lead rank (or play a wild) wins all cards in the trick.",
